\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  When the Lord is on my side,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I fear no evil one.
\par When I call upon the Lord,
\par They stumble and fall down.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par They Lord is my companion,
\par His love keeps me each day.
\par No group of hostile for us
\par Can cause me any harm
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I know, and I do believe,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And I am hopeful too,
\par That my God who's in heaven
\par Shall give me happiness.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When any harm befalls me,
\par He'll be with me always.
\par When the storm rise against me
\par He'll quickly subdue it.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My unyielding foundation
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Is the blood of Jesus.
\par That is my precious treasure,
\par And salvation as well.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par There is nothing just like it,
\par In all aspects of life.
\par And I am content to have
\par What e'er Christ has for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus the source of my pride,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  My glory and my light.
\par  I would not come, a loner,
\par  If Jesus were not mine,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par To stand before the mighty God,
\par  In request for His grace.
\par  I'm like a leaf that is dried,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 And burnt in fiery flame.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  His soul lives within my heart,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 And overrules my thoughts
\par I'm saddled with no problems,
\par And I enjoy my peace
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In all that He does for me,
\par Prosperity is mine
\par My heart receives a booster,
\par boldly I say "Abba"
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  Should anything frighten me,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Should I become afraid,
\par It's He who gives me courage
\par Out of His holy words.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Should things become difficult,
\par And be beyond reasoning;
\par He who sees into all hearts,
\par Knows about everything.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  7.  When someone walks with Jesus,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Satan greatly hates him,
\par He, with extremes of hatred,
\par Persecute the faithful.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He leads into temptation
\par And bring him to disgrace,
\par But the pow'r of the Lords' cross
\par Is worthless unto him.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  8.   Neither angels nor powers,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Glories nor monarchies,
\par Contentment, destitution,
\par Happiness, frightfulness,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Neither things small nor things great,
\par Things of this worldly life,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1 Nor any personal treasures,\cf0 
\par Can draw me from His side.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  9.  Rejoicing within my heart,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Shall increase day by day!
\par It's filled with great happiness,
\par And songs of extreme joy.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par My sunshine of liberation
\par Is Jesus Christ, the Lord.
\par And it's the  wealth of heaven,
\par \pard     That makes me sing his praise.\f1\fs17 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

